2. c4
{ [%eval -0.14] [%cal Gc4d5] The Réti. Instead of building a pawn centre, White attacks d5 from the side. This is the hypermodern idea: let Black occupy the centre, and then put pressure on it. If Black takes on c4, White gets the pawn back without trouble. }
2... e6 { [%eval 0.24] Black defends d5 solidly. } ( 2... d4
{ [%eval -0.10] Black gains space and keeps the position closed, a bit like a Benoni with the colours reversed. White attacks the pawn with the solid e3; the sharp 3.b4 is also possible, a kind of Benko Gambit. }
3. e3 { [%eval -0.19] White hits the pawn on d4. } 3... Nc6
